-- title:
--   Order zero at an ordinary point for the ∞-branch reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of an algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\mathbb Q$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$(1\cdot q)$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$. Assume: (h₁) the Laurent series $f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation, away from the kernel of coefficientwise reduction, of the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at level $1\cdot q$; (h₁F) the image $\pi(f)$ of $f$ under the induced homomorphism `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom (1 * q) A.toSubring red` into $k(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of $k(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`; (h₁0) $\pi(f) \neq 0$. Let $a \in k$ with $a \notin$ `ssJSet q k`; that is, some Weierstrass curve over $k$ that is elliptic has $j$-invariant $a$ and carries a nonzero point killed by $q$. Assume finally (hsupp) that for every place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a valuation subring containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, proper, and a principal ideal ring) with $\mathrm{ord}_W(f) \neq 0$, it fails that both: there is $x \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}(x) = a$ and $\mathrm{ord}_W(j - x) > 0$, where $j$ is the coefficientwise image of the series `jq`, and there is $y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}(y) = a^q$ and $\mathrm{ord}_W(j_q - y) > 0$, where $j_q$ is the coefficientwise image of `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq`. Here $\mathrm{ord}_W$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation. Then $\pi(f)$, viewed as an element of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, has order $0$ at the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a`, the place obtained by transporting the finite place of $k(T)$ attached to $T - a$.
--
--   This is the local statement, at an ordinary $j$-value $a$ in characteristic $q$, that the $\infty$-branch reduction of a function on $X_0(q)_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ which is a unit there has neither zero nor pole: on the integral model the special fibre consists of two copies of the $j$-line crossing at the supersingular points, so a point of the first component with ordinary $j$-invariant does not lie on the second, and a divisor supported away from it cannot contribute. It is used in the treatment of place specialisations and of the prolongation tuples attached to the two branches, in particular in the analysis of functions fixed by the Fricke involution.
